ndler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/15/DSC09842.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. (Oct. 15, 2026) – The No. 12-ranked West Virginia University women's soccer team caps a three-game homestand when it welcomes UCF to Morgantown on Friday, Oct. 16. The match is part of a double header with the WVU men's soccer team, and kickoff at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium is set for 3 p.m. ET.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/15/DSC09842.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/15/DSC09842.jpg"><media:title>Layla Thompson dribbles the ball during a match at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/15/DSC09842.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:46:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>13</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59547</s:story_id></item><item><title>Muller and Syrja Make Finals at ISSF World Cup</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/15/rifle-muller-and-syrja-make-finals-at-issf-world-cup</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/15/rifle-muller-and-syrja-make-finals-at-issf-world-cup</guid><category>Rifle</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Lauri Syrja and Oceanne Muller compete at the WVU Rifle season opening event" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/15/Syrja_and_Muller.png" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – Oceanne Muller and Lauri Syrja highlighted the Mountaineers in action at the 2026 ISSF World Cup in Cairo, Egypt, as the pair each qualified for one final at the event. Muller competed for France, Syrja for Finland, as Griffin Lake and Ashlyn Blake each competed for the United States.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/15/Syrja_and_Muller.png" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/15/Syrja_and_Muller.png"><media:title>Lauri Syrja and Oceanne Muller compete at the WVU Rifle season opening event</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/15/Syrja_and_Muller.png" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:38:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>8</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59545</s:story_id></item><item><title>West Virginia Set to Host Kentucky</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/15/mens-soccer-west-virginia-set-to-host-kentucky</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/15/mens-soccer-west-virginia-set-to-host-kentucky</guid><category>Men's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Pablo Pozos battles for the ball against South Carolina" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/15/MSOC_VS_USC__61_large.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The No. 24 West Virginia University men's soccer team welcomes Kentucky, Friday, Oct. 16, for a Sun Belt matchup. Kickoff from Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium is set for 7 p.m.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/15/MSOC_VS_USC__61_large.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/15/MSOC_VS_USC__61_large.jpg"><media:title>Pablo Pozos battles for the ball against South Carolina</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/15/MSOC_VS_USC__61_large.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:07:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>6</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59543</s:story_id></item><item><title>WVU Falls to No. 1-Seeded Oklahoma State in Playoff Tiebreaker at Big 12 Match Play Championship</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/14/golf-wvu-falls-to-no-1-seeded-oklahoma-state-in-playoff-tiebreaker-at-big-12-match-play-championship</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/14/golf-wvu-falls-to-no-1-seeded-oklahoma-state-in-playoff-tiebreaker-at-big-12-match-play-championship</guid><category>Golf</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Jack Michael lines up a putt" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/14/10142026.GOLF.BIG12.ES.001.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The West Virginia University golf team tied No. 7-ranked and 12-time National Champion Oklahoma State, 2.5-2.5, before falling to the Cowboys in a playoff tiebreaker at the Big 12 Match Play Championship in Salt Lake City on Wednesday.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/14/10142026.GOLF.BIG12.ES.001.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/14/10142026.GOLF.BIG12.ES.001.jpg"><media:title>Jack Michael lines up a putt</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/14/10142026.GOLF.BIG12.ES.001.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:50:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>5</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59542</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Head to ITA Atlantic Regional Championships</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/14/tennis-mountaineers-head-to-ita-atlantic-regional-championships</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/14/tennis-mountaineers-head-to-ita-atlantic-regional-championships</guid><category>Tennis</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Daniela Gonzales awaits a serve during a match at the Martha Thorn Invitational." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/14/VVB06369.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The West Virginia University tennis team travels to Lynchburg, Va., for the ITA Atlantic Regional Championships on Oct. 15-19.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/14/VVB06369.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/14/VVB06369.jpg"><media:title>Daniela Gonzales awaits a serve during a match at the Martha Thorn Invitational.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/14/VVB06369.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 14:01:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>15</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59541</s:story_id></item><item><title>Nickel Tabbed Big 12 Co-Offensive Player of the Week</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/14/womens-soccer-nickel-tabbed-big-12-co-offensive-player-of-the-weeknickel-tabbed-big-12-co-offensive-player-of-the-week</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/14/womens-soccer-nickel-tabbed-big-12-co-offensive-player-of-the-weeknickel-tabbed-big-12-co-offensive-player-of-the-week</guid><category>Women's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Sophia Nickel celebrates after a goal." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/14/WSoc_WVUvsBYU_Oct8_2026_TT-1__1_.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – After helping the Mountaineers earn their second ranked win of the season, junior forward/defender Sophia Nickel of the No. 12-ranked West Virginia University women's soccer team has been named the Big 12 Conference Co-Offensive Player of the Week, as announced by the league on Wednesday.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/14/WSoc_WVUvsBYU_Oct8_2026_TT-1__1_.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/14/WSoc_WVUvsBYU_Oct8_2026_TT-1__1_.jpg"><media:title>Sophia Nickel celebrates after a goal.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/14/WSoc_WVUvsBYU_Oct8_2026_TT-1__1_.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:00:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>13</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59540</s:story_id></item><item><title>United Bank Playbook: Impressive Ground Attacks on Display Saturday</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/14/football-impressive-ground-attacks-to-be-on-display-saturday-afternoon</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/14/football-impressive-ground-attacks-to-be-on-display-saturday-afternoon</guid><category>Football</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Quarterback Michael Hawkins Jr. runs the football during practice on the Steve Antoline Family Practice Facility on Tuesday, October. 13, as West Virginia prepares to face Cincinnati on Saturday in Milan Puskar Stadium." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/14/Hawkins-Practice_0LZql.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – Two of the top rushing teams in the Big 12 Conference will meet Saturday afternoon at high noon when West Virginia faces Cincinnati in a H